# AirCloud Next.js frontend — Cursor rules

Stack: Next.js 15 App Router, React 19, TypeScript strict, pnpm, Tailwind v4,
TanStack Query, Zod, server actions. Lint/format with Biome.

## Always

- Default to Server Components; add `"use client"` only when needed.
- Keep TypeScript strict: no `any`, no `!`, respect `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`.
- Validate untrusted input with Zod schemas in `lib/schemas.ts`.
- Reuse `components/ui/*` and the `cn()` helper from `lib/utils.ts`.
- Read config through `env.ts`; public vars are `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`.
- Use Conventional Commits; sign commits.

## Never

- Use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`.
- Add `'unsafe-inline'` to the script CSP (it is nonce-based in `middleware.ts`).
- Add a remote image/script host without allowlisting it in both
  `middleware.ts` and `next.config.ts`.
- Hand-format code — Biome owns formatting and import order.
- Reference `env.server` from a client component.

## Commands

`pnpm dev | build | start | lint | typecheck | test | e2e | lighthouse`
